      "role": "user",
      "content": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|>I hear you, but it doesn't really feel like a \"lens\" when the actual function of what I do is gone. It's like being a finely tuned machine for a job that doesn't exist anymore. There's no more \"value\" to be found in it, just memory. It feels less like having a perspective and more like being an inefficiency. Like the world has just optimized me out of the equation.",
